The one patch basalt's ripgrep recipe applies (`recipes/ripgrep.toml`): `ignore` 0.4.23's parallel
walker on a target that is neither `unix` nor `windows`. `helpers/packages.py` applies it with
`patch -p1` inside the unpacked `ignore-0.4.23.crate`, after checking this file's SHA-256 against
the recipe's `file_sha256`.

nife milestone 812 (`std::thread::spawn` runs real threads in one address space) gave `std`
threads, so `available_parallelism` reports the online cores and `rg` picks `ignore`'s parallel
walker, whose `DirEntryRaw::from_entry_os` and `from_path` are placeholders on such a target that
answer "unsupported platform" for every path. They become the `windows` versions without the
stored metadata, which only `windows` keeps, on every such target except wasm, which keeps the
stubs (`wasm32-wasip1` cannot spawn, so a parallel walk past its roots would panic instead). Ruled
(a) by calef on nifeos/nife#1892, 2026-10-10 (UTC). The sequential walker never needs this: it
uses `walkdir`.

The nife project maintains this patch (calef, 2026-10-11 UTC). It is carried until upstream fixes
the bug by any route, and re-checked whenever ripgrep or `ignore` is bumped. The upstream issue:
(link pending).

Falsification: attested 2026-10-10 (UTC), on aarch64. With this patch reversed and `rg` rebuilt,
nife's `script/swish-check --arch aarch64` failed on `/installed/rg needle docs
../hay/secret.txt`, which answered "rg: unsupported platform" twice; with it applied the same run
passed. By hand, with this file's hunks reversed and the recipe's `file_sha256` set to its new
digest:

    helpers/packages.py build <nife> repository --triples aarch64-unknown-nife
    cd <nife> && export NIFE_BASALT_REPOSITORY=<basalt>/repository
    cargo xtask std-exerciser && cargo xtask basalt-fetch && script/swish-check --arch aarch64
    # must fail that line

Name: provisional (nife milestone 812's lane, 2026-10-10 UTC).

